-- title:
--   Uniform oracle charges add across a finite loop
-- statement:
--   Let $B$ be any state type, let $f(j,b)$ be a charged computation returning a state in $B$ for every $j\in\mathbb N$ and $b\in B$, and let $k\in\mathbb N$. Write $Q(A)$ for the sum of the two independence-oracle charge counters of a computation $A$. Assume $Q(f(j,b))\le k$ for every index and input state. For every loop length $N\in\mathbb N$ and initial state $b$, sequentially applying the bodies at indices $0,\ldots,N-1$ gives $$Q(\operatorname{repeatFor}(f,N,b))\le Nk.$$ This is the uniform composition rule for oracle budgets.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/meelgroup/counting-matroid/blob/dd16a4628fdb095c58fe0f3dfd8e353c6e97443c/CountingMatroid/Analysis/BoundedRunOracleCalls.lean#L19-L44

